{
  "_comment": [
    "Phase API-4D §7 — cross-SDK metadata wire fixtures.",
    "Every Valori SDK maps an ergonomic metadata mapping to the canonical wire",
    "form the OpenAPI contract requires. `POST /v1/records` commits those bytes",
    "INSIDE the InsertRecord event, so they are covered by the BLAKE3 audit",
    "chain: two SDKs writing the same metadata must produce the same bytes, or",
    "the same logical write yields two different state hashes.",
    "",
    "`json` is the canonical serialisation (JSON.stringify semantics: no",
    "whitespace, real UTF-8, insertion order). `bytes` is its UTF-8 encoding —",
    "the `list[int]` that POST /v1/records takes. Batch-insert takes `json`.",
    "",
    "Read by sdk/python/tests/test_metadata_wire.py and",
    "sdk/typescript/tests/wire-parity.test.ts. A new SDK adds a reader here,",
    "not a second hand-written table of expectations."
  ],
